{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added a nullable `word_count` column to `entries` and exposed it as `word_count` on the API entry object. The build and existing tests pass; nothing exercises the new field yet.\n\n- **Storage:** the count is computed in the storage layer on every path that writes entry content (`createEntry`, `updateEntry`, `UpdateEntryTitleAndContent`), so new and updated entries are always populated. Words are whitespace-separated tokens of the content after `sanitizer.StripTags`.\n- **Existing entries:** not backfilled; the migration adds the column with no default, so they stay null until they are next saved.\n- **API:** `model.Entry` gains `WordCount *int` (`json:\"word_count\"`), read by the entry query builder; the Go client's `Entry` has the same field.\n- **Annotation:** the new helper `countContentWords` has no `@effects` tag, because `StripTags`, which it calls, is itself untagged.\n- **Not changed:** the webhook payload does not include the word count.", "t": 1794461782.316}
